A||||17||rodmcneill||Difference between 86 GT-87GT||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||03-16-2001||09:34 AM||||How can you tell the difference between a 86 GT from a 87 GT, just looking at them from the outside. Blue color not included(87 only)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||03-16-2001||09:43 AM||||You can't.  Pop the decklid, if the plenum has Fiero engraved into it it's 87-88, if it's a sticker it's an 86.  If it's a 4 speed it's an 86, but about 2,200 late 86 GT's got the 5 speed.  <P>As far as the exterior goes, all fastback GT's are pretty much the same.<P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information<BR>        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: SavedByJebus    -- you'll understand if you watch The Simpsons :D||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||03-16-2001||09:58 AM||||Between 86 and 87 no external differences.<BR>88 had different wheel width in front. Noticed by the silver edge. The 88's didn't have silver trim on bottom.<BR>Mechanically most 86 GT's had 4-spd but some got the 5-spd near the end of the 86 production run. Plenum is engraved on 87/88.<BR>88 doesn't use the cooling blower and pipes for the alternator and coil. 87/88 had 1 gallon bigger gas tank.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cifc||03-16-2001||11:16 AM||||I think that some of the 86 GT's also had engraved plenums.  I had one that did.  I've also seen a couple at shows.<BR>--Jason||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||03-16-2001||11:42 AM||||I'm pretty sure the silver skirt accents were differen't shades between '86-'87. I think '87 is darker shade?||||reg||1
Z||000005||kslish||03-16-2001||11:58 AM||||This one is obvious:  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>How about looking at the year letter contained in the VIN number tag at the base of the windshield?  <P>The model year code is the 10th digit in the VIN number....<P>G = 86, H = 87<P>Gotta love that handy pocket Fiero Spotters Guide for this kind of info.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||03-16-2001||12:00 PM||||Bob Englert has a couple of '87 GT's, and I have compared them to my '86.  i have noticed that:<P><B>1)</B>the '87's are missing the heat deflector, located above the muffler, and below the coil/altenator cooling tubes.  <P><B>2)</B>there is also a channel, located in the tire well wall, that runs underneath the battery tray, back towards the altenator.  my '86 has a coolant tube in there, and Bob's '87's don't.  it appears that there is some differnce in the coolant tube layout's.<P><B>3)</B>also, don't forget the '87's have there "special" upgraded headlight motors (can you tell i'm jealous?)<P>and if your curious, my car is a june '86 GT with a 5 speed, and i have compared them to a '87 5 speed and automatic!<P>i know there are other differnce's... i just haven't found yet.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000007||frontal lobe||03-16-2001||12:20 PM||||I have had an '86GT and an '87GT.  My '86GT had plain black door handles.  My '87GT has door handles that say "Fiero" on them.  Is that the way they all are?  I just assumed, but now I'm not sure.||||reg||1
Z||000008||87GT||03-16-2001||01:55 PM||||I have a 87 and there isnt fiero stickers on the handles.  I dont think Ive ever seen those.  Medium Red Metallic is also a color seen on 87s and not on 86s.  So if you see a Med Red fiero with the silver trim on the bottom, then its definately a 87GT.  Maroon was on 88s as well, but they are a solid color and with black or gold rims.  Im pretty sure all 86 and 87GTs had silver rims.||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||03-16-2001||02:36 PM||||Well, if you see one with a rack on the back like so, for sure it's an 86.  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=16712376&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||My7Fieros||03-16-2001||02:41 PM||||87s also started putting vin stickers on most every body panel. Either open the door, the hood, decklid, or better yet, if the car dosnt have a license plate on it, you'll see the vin sticker. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||frontal lobe||03-16-2001||03:20 PM||||Oops.  I just went out to the Fiero '87GT to check and the door handles have a clear cover and PONTIAC (not Fiero as I mistakenly put) right under the clear cover.  Isn't that what all '87GT's have on their door handles??||||reg||1
Z||000012||tgowens||03-16-2001||04:22 PM||||frontal........that was something that a previous owner added -- all door handles are the same......<P>As for the exterior differences.....the only difference is the shade of gray of the ground effects trim......'86 is a darker medium gray  (almost a flat tone) and the '87 is a lighter gray metallic....the rest of the differences, plenum, headlight motors etc. are internal||||reg||1
Z||000013||frontal lobe||03-16-2001||04:44 PM||||Thanks tgowens.  I never knew.  The handles looked like stock ones would-not like a cheap add-on, so I had just assumed that it was a minor model year change from '86 to '87.  Hmmm, so the neon running lights, curb feelers, and fuzzy dice aren't stock '87 features either????  (joking, mine DOES NOT have those)||||reg||1
Z||000014||Shiner||03-16-2001||11:28 PM||||Well, my '87 GT has the "PONTIAC" door handle emblems, and neither of the other Fieros have them.  It REALLY doesn't look like a cheap aftermarket thing to me.<P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000015||fiero56||03-16-2001||11:53 PM||||Probably off of an f-body.||||reg||1
Z||000016||rockcrawl||03-17-2001||07:39 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>2)there is also a channel, located in the tire well wall, that runs underneath the battery tray, back towards the altenator. my '86 has a coolant tube in there, and Bob's '87's don't. it appears that there is some differnce in the coolant tube layout's<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is correct, the '87s have the heater return line combined with the rh coolant return. you can see the heater hose going into the larger coolant pipe. So up until '86 there were 4 coolant tubes running the length of the car, and in '87 there were only three.<P>I almost forgot, the clutch master cyl design changed, but I think that was mid '86. Of course you can't see that without opening the hood.<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 03-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Kelvin Vivian||03-17-2001||12:00 PM||||Another difference (though not visible on the outside) between an 86 GT and an 87 GT would be a larger gas tank...<P>87 and 88 Fieros have a 11.9 gal tank vs. the 10.2 gal. tank of the 84-86 year Fieros. <P>Kelvin<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd, med red met/gray<BR>88 GT T-top, 5-spd, bright red/tan<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/no_18/finalfront.jpg">  1987 SE 4-cyl, 5 spd||||reg||1
